LobsterAI: isolate SQLite read-only worker results from native stdout noise.

Windows process hooks can append diagnostics to stdout even after a successful
worker exit. Send the result through a per-call private file, retaining strict
JSON/result validation, nonzero-exit handling, and temporary-file cleanup.
Rebuild the parent and worker together; there is deliberately no stdout fallback.
Retire when the pinned upstream worker protocol isolates its structured results.

